<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>DrakeForge</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: dark; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    padding: 24px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 10%, #4a0000 0, #0a0a0a 55%, #050505 100%);
    color: #f0f0f0;
    font: 15px/1.55 system-ui, sans-serif;
  }
  main {
    max-width: 34rem;
    padding: 26px;
    border: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: rgba(13, 13, 13, 0.92);
  }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 21px; }
  p { margin: 0 0 14px; color: #aaaaaa; }
  strong { color: #f0f0f0; }
  a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e60012, #4a0000);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  code { color: #ff4d5a; }
  .note { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12px; color: #666666; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<!--
  Canonical Dragon86 app shortcut. The filename `drakeforge.d86` matches the
  `drakeforge` entry in Dragon86's iframe-apps.json, so the OS app launcher
  opens its built-in new-tab launcher. This HTML is also a standalone pointer
  when viewed directly: it never embeds or recreates the DrakeForge IDE.
-->
<main>
  <h1>DrakeForge opens in a separate tab</h1>
  <p>
    This app shortcut launches DrakeForge's existing standalone BrowserCode UI at
    <code>/DrakeForge/standalone</code> in a <strong>top-level browser tab</strong>.
    No iframe, no copied IDE components, and no cross-origin-isolation requirement
    is placed on Dragon86 or the PS1 emulator. The standalone tab establishes the
    COOP/COEP that BrowserPod needs for <code>SharedArrayBuffer</code>.
  </p>
  <a
    id="drakeforge-launch"
    href="https://dragon-gaming-platforms.github.io/DrakeForge/standalone"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    data-launch-mode="separate-top-level-tab"
  >Open DrakeForge in a new tab</a>
  <p class="note">
    Standalone mode uses DrakeForge's own 9p Worker and IndexedDB; it does not
    connect to Dragon86's <code>fs1</code> filesystem. Launch this as an app
    shortcut, not from the Files app's sandboxed HTML preview.
  </p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
